data/corpus.json.gz redistributes verbatim excerpts of KEP prose — specifically the
"Alternatives", "Drawbacks" and "Risks and Mitigations" sections — together with structured
metadata from kep.yaml and OWNERS files.

Modifications made to that material:
  - HTML comments stripped (the KEP template's own prompts)
  - "Alternatives" sections split into individual titled options
  - structural sub-headings ("Examples", "Conclusion", "Implementation sketch") excluded
  - OWNERS group aliases expanded to individual handles via OWNERS_ALIASES
  - bot accounts filtered
  - email addresses NOT ingested, by choice

No personal data beyond the GitHub handles, display names and affiliations that the Kubernetes
project itself publishes as its governance record is included.
